From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dilip Dalton <dilipdalton@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:59:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvmf: name the listener address when a host is refused

"Subsystem does not allow host to connect at this address" did not say
which address. Name the listener (trtype/traddr/trsvcid) so an
unexpected refusal can be traced to the listener that refused it.

Flint-only (diagnostics). test/unit/lib/nvmf/ctrlr.c/ctrlr_ut does not
link with this change (it needs a spdk_nvme_transport_id_trtype_str
stub); the image is built without unit tests.

Formerly spdk-csi-driver/nvmf-hostlog.patch.
---
 lib/nvmf/ctrlr.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/nvmf/ctrlr.c b/lib/nvmf/ctrlr.c
index dafaa7ddc..519fc7e8f 100644
--- a/lib/nvmf/ctrlr.c
+++ b/lib/nvmf/ctrlr.c
@@ -857,8 +857,9 @@ nvmf_qpair_access_allowed(struct spdk_nvmf_qpair *qpair, struct spdk_nvmf_subsys
 	}
 
 	if (!spdk_nvmf_subsystem_listener_allowed(subsystem, &listen_trid)) {
-		SPDK_ERRLOG("Subsystem '%s' does not allow host '%s' to connect at this address.\n",
-			    subsystem->subnqn, hostnqn);
+		SPDK_ERRLOG("Subsystem '%s' does not allow host '%s' to connect at this address. Listener address is %s/%s/%s\n",
+			    subsystem->subnqn, hostnqn, spdk_nvme_transport_id_trtype_str(listen_trid.trtype),
+			    listen_trid.traddr, listen_trid.trsvcid);
 		return false;
 	}
 
